Declarations are private by default. In `@mod.moth` and `@package.moth`, place `$export` before each public declaration or direct-selection re-export.

### Exporting declarations

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    private_helper || -> String:
        return "private"
    ;

    $export
    public_name #= "Moth"

    $export
    render || -> String:
        return private_helper()
    ;
]

`$export` applies only to the next eligible item. It occupies its own line and a blank line breaks attachment. A `#` binding is compile-time, not automatically public.

### Re-exporting helpers

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    $export
    @components/card CardData as Card, render_card
]

This publishes `Card` and `render_card`. `CardData` is not also exported under its original name.

Files within a module can bind shared helpers. Other modules see only the matching facade's exported API. Declarations in separate root files remain isolated. Public signatures cannot expose private types or trait evidence, and public callables require closed error contracts.

See @#public-api (Public API) and @../packages/#module-visibility (Module visibility).
